WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.770
Imagine a finance minister who
takes no new decisions all year.

2
00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:05.980
No tax rises.

3
00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:07.290
No tax cuts.

4
00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:09.190
No new spending plans.

5
00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:11.350
Then a recession hits.

6
00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:12.440
By the end of the year,

7
00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:14.620
government borrowing has jumped.

8
00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:17.850
So why does a government's
borrowing jump in a recession,

9
00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:20.190
even when nobody votes for it?

10
00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:22.800
In this mission, you'll
use a graph lab and watch

11
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:25.520
a fall in spending pass
through the economy,

12
00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:27.130
round by round.

13
00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:31.700
Then you'll test the rules some governments
set to limit their own borrowing.

14
00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:35.240
Your mission: find out what
pushes borrowing up when

15
00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:36.520
no one decides to.
